==English==

===Etymology 1===
In {{onomatopoeic|en|title=imitation}} of a cry. Used since at least the 18th century.<ref>{{R:OCD2|page=1}}</ref> Compare {{m|en|ah}}, of which it could be a lengthened form.

====Pronunciation====
* {{IPA|en|/ɑː(ɹ)(ɡ)/|qual2=natural exclamation|[ɑɹɣ]|[ɑːɣː]}}
* {{audio|en|en-ca-argh.ogg|a=CA}}
* {{rhymes|en|ɑː(ɹ)ɡ|s=1}}

====Interjection====
{{en-interj}}

# {{lb|en|onomatopoeia}} {{non-gloss|Expressing [[annoyance]], [[dismay]], [[embarrassment]] or [[frustration]].}}
#: {{ux|en|'''Argh!''' Itʼs already 7:15! Weʼre never gonna make it!}}

=====Usage notes=====
Any of the letters may be reduplicated, e.g. ''Arrggh!'', ''Aaaarrrggghhh!'', ''Aarrghh!''

